{
  "$schema": "https://emdashcms.com/seed.schema.json",
  "version": "1",
  "meta": {
    "name": "Songhealth CMS Content Model",
    "description": "The Songhealth content model (current/02-content-model.md): eleven native collections (documents, pages, news, activities, announcements, health_content, services, health_reports, personnel, health_services and moit) with their fields, three block types (ita_requirement, ita_file and ita_link), six relations (document_successor, page_documents, announcement_documents, service_documents, report_document and facility_services) and nine taxonomies (topic, audience, the hierarchical area, document_type, news_category, announcement_type, service_category, report_type and facility_type). Domain dates such as activity_at stay separate from native publication and scheduling, and no date unpublishes anything. A Health Report describes the one Document it requires; a Service is guidance only, with no transaction or payment. The nine public collections carry their canonical URL patterns (current/03 §15) and SEO support. A MOIT entry is one indicator of one fiscal year's ITA, at /ita/{slug} with SEO, and its Evidence is a blocks field of Requirement, file and link blocks, each piece of Evidence with a Round (spec #121, ADR 0006). Personnel is not routable, because no per-person public route exists (03 §5). The Admin sidebar puts the collections in folders by domain, ordered by use, each with an icon; Documents is in no folder (#169). The seed defines only the Document Type reference terms policy, plan and result, and the three Homepage menus staff curate (homepage-featured, homepage-services and homepage-quick-access), empty; it defines no other terms and no redirects, widget areas, sections or content: term inventories wait for authoritative sources. Area terms model Province, District, Subdistrict and Village, with the official code in the term slug, the name in its label and the parent through native group identity. EmDash applies this seed only when it sets up a fresh database; an existing database gets later model changes from scripts/model-update.mjs."
  },
